WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.167
The sun sets.

2
00:00:04.168 --> 00:00:08.296
Wolves howl at the rising moon.

3
00:00:08.297 --> 00:00:12.924
Owls' hoots echo through the night.

4
00:00:12.925 --> 00:00:16.528
Bats swoop through the darkness on silent wings.

5
00:00:16.529 --> 00:00:22.830
These creatures of the night are the stuff of spooky legends—and scary movies.

6
00:00:22.831 --> 00:00:27.370
But is there any truth to the legends surrounding these animals?

7
00:00:27.371 --> 00:00:32.463
Long ago it was frightening to hear wolves howling at night.

8
00:00:32.464 --> 00:00:40.124
Wolves were seen as dangerous beasts, and people who did horrible things were thought of as beasts.

9
00:00:40.125 --> 00:00:48.754
So legends arose of werewolves—people who turned into wolf-like beasts during a full moon.

10
00:00:48.755 --> 00:00:54.725
These werewolves had sharp fangs and claws and hairy bodies.

11
00:00:54.726 --> 00:01:09.129
They remained vicious beasts until the sun rose, when they returned to their human forms and personalities.

12
00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:11.948
Today we know that werewolves aren't real.

13
00:01:11.949 --> 00:01:16.337
We also know that wolves don't howl at night to be scary.

14
00:01:16.338 --> 00:01:20.094
Wolves are nocturnal, so they're awake at night.

15
00:01:20.095 --> 00:01:25.422
They howl to communicate with their pack or stake out territory.

16
00:01:25.423 --> 00:01:33.121
Pointing their noses toward the sky helps their sounds carry for a long distance—9 to 16 kilometers.

17
00:01:33.122 --> 00:01:38.348
Despite the legends, wolves don't howl more during full moons.

18
00:01:38.349 --> 00:01:43.463
People were just more likely to see wolves under the light of a full moon!

19
00:01:43.464 --> 00:01:48.392
The hoot of the owl also struck terror in people long ago.

20
00:01:48.393 --> 00:01:54.670
As with wolves, spooky legends arose about these mysterious nighttime creatures.

21
00:01:54.671 --> 00:01:58.875
In some legends witches turned into owls at night.

22
00:01:58.876 --> 00:02:02.903
Many cultures saw owls as a symbol of death.

23
00:02:02.904 --> 00:02:09.006
In Europe, for example, people believed that an owl nearby meant someone would die.

24
00:02:09.007 --> 00:02:14.978
When they heard the owl hoot, they hoped its big shiny eyes were not watching them!

25
00:02:14.979 --> 00:02:20.201
Luckily owls don't hoot at night as messengers of doom.

26
00:02:20.202 --> 00:02:24.150
Owls, like wolves, are nocturnal.

27
00:02:24.151 --> 00:02:27.998
They hoot to communicate with other owls. They

28
00:02:27.999 --> 00:02:33.983
may hoot to claim territory or talk to a mate or their chicks. Sometimes

29
00:02:33.984 --> 00:02:36.407
their hoots are warnings. But

30
00:02:36.408 --> 00:02:39.251
these aren't warnings of death. These

31
00:02:39.252 --> 00:02:46.951
warning hoots let other owls know there are people nearby! Why

32
00:02:46.952 --> 00:02:51.649
do owls have such large eyes that glow in the darkness? Since

33
00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:56.331
owls hunt at night, their eyes help them see. Owls

34
00:02:56.332 --> 00:03:00.776
can also turn their necks so they can see backwards. This

35
00:03:00.777 --> 00:03:06.175
helps them silently track their prey. Another

36
00:03:06.176 --> 00:03:13.378
creature of legend is the vampire bat—the strange flying mammal that sucks blood. Surprisingly,

37
00:03:13.379 --> 00:03:18.644
legends about vampires didn't come from vampire bats. People

38
00:03:18.645 --> 00:03:25.797
from Ancient Egypt, Tibet, and Rome had stories about vampires who sucked blood. Much

39
00:03:25.798 --> 00:03:33.826
later, European explorers discovered bats in Mexico and Central America that lived off blood. They

40
00:03:33.827 --> 00:03:39.684
named these bats vampire bats after the legendary creatures. The

41
00:03:39.685 --> 00:03:46.168
legend about human vampires turning into vampire bats began even later. That

42
00:03:46.169 --> 00:03:51.300
legend is from Dracula , the famous horror novel.

43
00:03:51.301 --> 00:03:56.575
The character Dracula could turn into a bat and fly through the night.

44
00:03:56.576 --> 00:04:02.297
But unlike vampires from legends, vampire bats don't really suck blood.

45
00:04:02.298 --> 00:04:09.437
Vampire bats usually approach their targets from the ground.

46
00:04:09.438 --> 00:04:13.987
They use their sharp teeth to pierce the skin of their prey.

47
00:04:13.996 --> 00:04:18.372
Then they drink the flowing blood using their tongues.

48
00:04:18.373 --> 00:04:22.438
They don't kill their victims—or turn them into vampires!

49
00:04:22.439 --> 00:04:25.858
And vampire bats rarely prey on humans.

50
00:04:25.859 --> 00:04:29.516
They usually feed on cattle and horses.

51
00:04:29.517 --> 00:04:33.262
People have always tried to explain the unknown.

52
00:04:33.263 --> 00:04:37.841
Legends help to explain mysterious things that people encounter.

53
00:04:37.842 --> 00:04:44.185
Now we know that some legends aren't true, but people still enjoy a good scary story.

54
00:04:44.186 --> 00:04:52.817
When the moon rises, filling the night with shadows, it's fun to pretend legends are real!

